# suite=machine; columns: <FAULT_ID> <must-fail> <allowed-prefixes> <must-pass>
# SHA-256 named faults (D-28, D-37, plan 03-02). Each id has one IVS_FAULT_<ID> site in
# core/src/common/ivs_sha256.c. Plan 03-09 hashes the machine state with this SHA-256, so a fault
# that changes the digest of the short preimages also breaks the literal digests of family digest
# (machine.digest.); only those three faults are widened, each for its own rule. Plan 03-10's
# load reports carry the SHA-256 of the supplied bytes, checked against literal digests, so the
# same three faults also break family load (machine.load.), again for their own rule.
SHA_K_WRONG machine.sha256.fips-abc machine.sha256.|machine.digest.|machine.load. machine.sha256.split-every-offset
SHA_ROTATE_WRONG machine.sha256.fips-448 machine.sha256.|machine.digest.|machine.load. machine.sha256.ctx-copy-snapshot
SHA_LENGTH_LE machine.sha256.pat-0001 machine.sha256.|machine.digest.|machine.load. machine.sha256.fips-empty
SHA_PAD_BOUNDARY machine.sha256.pat-0056 machine.sha256. machine.sha256.pat-0057
SHA_FINAL_BLOCK_DROPPED machine.sha256.pat-0063 machine.sha256. machine.sha256.pat-0055
SHA_INIT_NO_RESET machine.sha256.init-resets machine.sha256. machine.sha256.fips-abc
